"answer": "Chemotherapy can harm healthy cells, leading to various side effects. Common side effects include mouth sores, fatigue, nausea and vomiting, pain, and hair loss [MLP-464]. The specific side effects you experience depend on the type and amount of chemotherapy received and how your body reacts. While these effects can be significant, healthy cells usually recover after treatment ends, meaning most side effects go away over time. It is recommended to talk with your health care provider about ways to prevent or control these side effects [MLP-464]."
}
